    "body": ".. and then get to a screeching halt just before actually to attempting to deeply refactor win_line() lmao. For now:\n\n- maintain a valid mb_schar_width to go along with mb_schar as we often can calculate the value earlier.\n\n- use a FAKE but valid `mb_c` value after we already have processed buffer and p_extra text and already have decided to put a replacement mb_schar onto the screen (often a list char or a conceal char)\n\n<!--\n  Thank you for contributing to Neovim!\n  If this is your first time, check out https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs\n  for our PR guidelines.\n-->\n\n## Problem\n\n## Solution\n",
